{"name":"Tarnished Epistles","hex":"#e6ddcd","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tarnished","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of tarnish"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Discolored or blemished.","Sullied or dishonored."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tarnished"},{"term":"epistles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of epistle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epistles"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tarnished","blocks":[{"text":"Tarnished is a 1950 American action film directed by Harry Keller, written by John K. Butler and starring Dorothy Patrick, Arthur Franz, Barbra Fuller and Jimmy Lydon. The film was released on February 28, 1950 by Republic Pictures. The screenplay is based on the novel Turn Home, written in 1945 by author Eleanor Mayo."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/Tarnished_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarnished","wikidata":"Q21647088"},{"title":"Epistle","blocks":[{"text":"An epistle is a writing directed or sent to a person or group of people, usually an elegant and formal didactic letter. The epistle genre of letter-writing was common in ancient Egypt as part of the scribal-school writing curriculum. The letters in the New Testament written by apostles to the early Christians are usually referred to as epistles; those traditionally attributed to Paul are known as Pauline epistles and the others as catholic epistles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/File%22-Saint_Paul_Writing_His_Epistles%22_by_Valentin_de_Boulogne.jpg/330px-File%22-Saint_Paul_Writing_His_Epistles%22_by_Valentin_de_Boulogne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epistle","wikidata":"Q215495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi